<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turkish War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Turkish War of Independence was fought by the Turkish nationalist movement under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a> against the Allied partition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> government defeated Armenian forces in the east, French forces in the south and Greek armies in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> of 1923 recognised the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turkish-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Turkish War of Independence" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lubunya · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C3%BCrk_Kurtulu%C5%9F_Sava%C5%9F%C4%B1_-_kolaj.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
